      "text": "Earlier this month, a U.S. Coast Guard Station Miami Beach LE crew assisted CBP Air and Marine Operations and Homeland Security Investigations special agents in the interdiction of suspected smuggling vessel.\n\nWorking together, we seized 245 pounds of cocaine valued at approximately $3.4 million from a 52-foot sailing vessel from Colombia, on April 5.\n\nThe Coast Guard continues to increase operations to interdict, seize, and disrupt transshipment of cocaine and other bulk illicit drugs by sea. These drugs fuel and enable cartels and Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCO) to produce and traffic illegal fentanyl threatening the U.S.\n\nWorking alongside our interagency partners, the men and women of the Coast Guard are doing everything in their power to interdict drugs before they reach our shores and our citizens.\n\n#Smuggler #USCG #Interdiction #DrugBust",
